{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/97362.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS DENO-DDB0E7: Treasure case 2005 T196, Roman silver TOT finger-ring from Scopwick, Lincolnshire"]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["anello"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (anello)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["200-300 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Lincolnshire (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Iscrizione o legenda"]},"value":{"none":["TOT"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["Silver intaglio finger ring with triangular shoulders, each decorated with angled incised lines. The ring has an applied circular disc on the bezel, inscribed 'TOT' with distinctive lettering. The ring is of the 'keeled' type with a distinctive carinated profile. Discussion. The ring's is Henig's Type VIII. The style of the inscription is virtually identical to that of a similar ring found in Lincolnshire (Johns 1996, 59, fig. 3.19). Date: 3rd century AD. Ext. d.: 18.2 mm x 19.0 mm; Int. d.: 14.0 mm x 14.2 mm; Wt.: 4.1g"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["DENO-DDB0E7"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["97362"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: The British Museum, Caroline Barton, 2012-04-17 17:33:11, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/97362","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS DENO-DDB0E7: Treasure case 2005 T196, Roman silver TOT finger-ring from Scopwick, Lincolnshire"]},"format":"text/html"}],"items":[{"id":"https://raw.git